														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2434881">
									

<p>I've already told you my general opinion personally but I'll put it here for the record: I really dig this. When things are built up for so long in the way the Misters are, with Redd as the big question mark, when you finally &quot;reveal the monster&quot; it will usually turn out to be disappointing compared to the hype. So I was really pleasantly surprised with how good this was.</p>
<p>It maintains a fitting, semi-surreal atmosphere that really works great for the piece as a whole, and every connection made to other works feels wholly deserved. Connections to the Scarlet King are the kind of thing that makes me afterwards think &quot;it makes so much sense, why didn't I think of that earlier?&quot;, which is pretty much perfect for a reveal.</p>
<p>I could probably go on for longer about why I think this is great, but it'd just tend into rambling: I really really like this.</p>

